This bit is worth repeating - Before you get your first
gift the number of existing artifacts has NO effect on the
odds of getting that first gift.  None whatsoever.  Artifacts
created in bones files or wishing, naming, dipping, death
drops, you name it, none are gifts and none effect the
chance of the first gift.

I just checked pray.c to see if crowning counts as a gift.
It does even if the gift is a spellbook.  So as far as I can
tell if you're stuck never getting an artifact from sacs
because of the eligibility rules, you can deliberately get
crowned, get your crowning gift and the other benefits
and that will release your restrictions.

Interestingly, getting crowned gives you a crowning artifact
not your classes guaranteed artifact and then the guaranteed
one is just one of many in the available ones.  A wizard
wanting Magicbane is well advised to go for it before getting
crowned.  A lawful valkyrie wanting to avoid Mjollnir may
want to deliberately get crowned before getting her first
gift from sacrafice.


